# Template for .devcontainer/monta-credentials.env, which is gitignored and must stay that way -
# these are live CSMS credentials.
#
# Copy this file to monta-credentials.env, fill it in, then run:
#
#     ./.devcontainer/monta-setup.sh              dry run, nothing reaches Monta
#     ./.devcontainer/monta-setup.sh --live       for real
#
# The station is three charge points, not one. A vSECC board serves two connectors, so a
# six-connector charger presents three separate OCPP identities and connector ids restart at 1 on
# each board. Create three charge points in Monta - OCPP 1.6J, security profile 2 - and paste the
# authorisation key it issues for each. They are not interchangeable: one key per charge point.

# Your prefix. The boards become <prefix>_1, _2, _3.
#
# USE YOUR OWN NAME. Two people running the same identity against the same Monta account displace
# each other's connections, and the one that loses sees only "Client closed, was not requested
# internally" in its log, which looks like a network fault rather than a colleague.
MONTA_PREFIX=YOURNAME_EVEREST

MONTA_KEY_1=
MONTA_KEY_2=
MONTA_KEY_3=

# Optional - defaults to 3, and must match the --vseccs the running config was generated with.
# MONTA_BOARDS=3

# The CSMS URL is NOT set here - it lives in .devcontainer/ocpp-monta.example.json, the template
# every board's config is generated from, along with the other forty settings that are identical
# across boards. Edit the template if it ever changes.
